[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114488,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Extraosseous ameloblastoma (EA) is the soft tissue counterpart of intraosseous ameloblastoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:26:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114489,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9310/0 Ameloblastoma, extraosseous/peripheral</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:26:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114490,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E83.0 &amp; XH1SV4 Benign osteogenic tumours of bone or articular cartilage of skull or face &amp; Ameloblastoma, NOS</p>\r\n<p>2E83.1 &amp; XH1SV4 Benign osteogenic tumours of bone or articular cartilage of lower jaw &amp; Ameloblastoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:26:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114491,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> soft tissue ameloblastoma; ameloblastoma of mucosal origin; ameloblastoma of the gingiva.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:26:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114492,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:26:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114493,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EA occurs only in soft tissues overlying tooth-bearing areas or edentulous ridges of the jaws, with a mandible-to-maxilla ratio of 1.6:1 to 3.3:1 {11120479; 8683419; 3295656; 16827840}. The most frequent subsites are the mandibular premolar and maxillary molar regions {3295656; 8683419; 11120479; 16827840; 29680843}; the lingual aspect of the alveolar ridge is often involved.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:26:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114494,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EA is an asymptomatic, slow-growing, firm epulis with a mean diameter of &lt;&nbsp;20&nbsp;mm {11120479; 29680843}.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>On imaging, superficial erosion of the underlying bone may be seen, but a central component precludes a diagnosis of EA.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:26:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114495,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EA accounts for as many as 10% of all ameloblastomas {11120479}. The mean patient age is 52&nbsp;years (range: 9&ndash;92&nbsp;years), with 64% of cases occurring during the fifth to seventh decades of life {11120479}. The M:F&nbsp;ratio is 1.4:1 {11120479}; however, a greater male predilection has been reported in some Asian series {11120479; 29680843}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:26:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114496,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Like other ameloblastomas, EA is probably caused by dysregulated MAPK signalling pathways.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:26:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114497,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "<p><em>BRAF</em> p.V600E mutations have been reported in 10&nbsp;of 16&nbsp;peripheral ameloblastoma cases {28658279; 29388014; 30811720; 33231757; 33827932}, with <em>NRAS</em> p.Q61R occurring in 1&nbsp;of 3&nbsp;cases {28658279}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T17:13:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114498,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EA is a firm to somewhat spongy mucosal mass, solid or with tiny cystic spaces {11120479; 29680843}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:26:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114499,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The histopathological features and growth patterns are the same as in conventional ameloblastoma {11120479}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>BerEP4 expression on immunohistochemistry may aid in distinguishing intraoral basal cell carcinoma from EA {29247621}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The differential diagnosis includes peripheral odontogenic fibroma, peripheral squamous odontogenic tumour, odontogenic gingival epithelial hamartoma, and intraoral basal cell carcinoma {11120479}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:26:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114500,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:26:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114501,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:26:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114502,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> site in the gingiva or edentulous alveolar mucosa; no intraosseous component; histopathological features of conventional ameloblastoma.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T17:14:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114503,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:26:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114504,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 137,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EA has a more indolent behaviour than conventional ameloblastoma {11120479}. Recurrence rates after conservative supraperiosteal excision range from 9% to 20%, although some recurrences may result from incomplete removal {33162201} and long-term follow-up is recommended. Malignant transformation is exceedingly rare {8426721}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:26:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]